L01 misconceptions:
   WRONG: Maximizing utility means buying as much of both goods as possible.
   WRONG: The marginal rate of substitution is always the ratio of the quantities of the two goods.
   WRONG: At any bundle on the budget line, the MRS equals the price ratio.
